{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/111910-changeling-regarding-modern-fae","id":111910,"title":"Changeling: Regarding \"Modern\" Fae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-12T22:23:26-07:00","id":111910,"title":"Changeling: Regarding \"Modern\" Fae","content":"The premise of Changeling is that the Fae were around, glamour disappeared, they left or underwent the Changeling Way, and finally they are struggling to continue to live in a starkly hostile world.<br /> <br /> So what happens with Fae like Gremlins. Gremlins are from WW2 and were held to be responsible for mechanical failures in aircraft. They would make perfect commoners with their knack for breaking things, but are also far too new to have undergone the Changeling Way. Given their relative youth, they probably find the modern world fairly hospitable.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of other modern Fae that are invented every day by humanity: things that steal socks, things that control traffic lights, etc. Do they not exist in the World of Darkness? Do they exist but just not interact with the older Fae? Are the older Fae jealous of them?<br /> <br /> Is there an Urban Court where Lord Neon and Lady Opera rule, unaffected by the banality that destroys their older cousins?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2481-lordofarcana","name":"LordofArcana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T23:06:37-07:00","id":111929,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordofArcana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/111910-changeling-regarding-modern-fae#post111910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what happens with Fae like Gremlins. Gremlins are from WW2 and were held to be responsible for mechanical failures in aircraft. They would make perfect commoners with their knack for breaking things, but are also far too new to have undergone the Changeling Way. Given their relative youth, they probably find the modern world fairly hospitable.<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> They\u2019re not called \u2018gremlins\u2019 per se, but the goblin kith fits that bill pretty nicely. Check out <i>Shadow Court</i>. They\u2019re the nocker Thallian, IIRC. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T03:56:41-07:00","id":113229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordofArcana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/111910-changeling-regarding-modern-fae#post111910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are plenty of other modern Fae that are invented every day by humanity: things that steal socks, things that control traffic lights, etc. Do they not exist in the World of Darkness? Do they exist but just not interact with the older Fae? Are the older Fae jealous of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things you describe here sound a lot more like Chimera than Fae, Fae aren't that easily created or born and no True Fae has been near the Autumn Realm since the Shattering. Chimerae on the other hand are born from human dreams and nightmares, they are the most likely culprits for stealing socks or messing with the traffick lights. And hte Fae, or rather Changelings are not envious of them but tend to either fight them, train them or befriend them as suits their nature. Many Changelings have Chimera companions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordofArcana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/111910-changeling-regarding-modern-fae#post111910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an Urban Court where Lord Neon and Lady Opera rule, unaffected by the banality that destroys their older cousins?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unseelie are more likely to hold urban Courts and tend to move more on the edge of human technology since such advancement is part of Unseelie nature where the Seelie tend towards more traditionalism. Also it is worth to remember that technology itself is not normally Banal, it can be but so can almost anything else under the correct circumstances, and can even be Glamorous. Unseelie Nockers, and the aforementioned Goblins (nicknamed Gremlins even in the books), tend to go with more modern, or even futuristic, aestethics to their technology which tends to work through Glamour infused in it and far exceed modern technology, which is true even of Seelie Nockers and their penchant for Steamtech, and other archaid, aestethics looks are hardly the defining feature in Fae technology. Lighting gun shoots out lightning whether it looks like an archaid dueling pistol or a sleek futurristic ray gun.<br /> <br /> Science is only Banal when it tries to destroy potential by creating limitations and rules and yet it can be Glamorous when used to discover new things and advancements on knowledge. This has never been more clear than with the moonlanding which opened flood gates of Glamour, that was science and technology that gave the world that huge Glamour filled morcel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T07:49:19-07:00","id":113319,"title":"","content":"I'm seconding everything Possessed said!<br /> <br /> If I recall correctly, back in the Dark Ages the version of chimera at the time could potentially gain enough substance and permanence to become full fledged fae. I could see something along those lines being theoretically still possible in the modern day, but it would be pretty much unheard of with how much banality permeates the world. Also, I don't think it would be possible for an individual chimera. It would need to be an entire race gaining enough substance and permanence in the Dreaming to become a new archetype. Essentially, it sounds like great fodder for long term chronicle to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there an Urban Court where Lord Neon and Lady Opera rule, unaffected by the banality that destroys their older cousins? </div> </div> </div>There's nothing to stop an individual of any of the existing kiths from taking on those sorts of titles and thriving on modern dreams. Nothing of the Dreaming is immune to banality though. Banality isn't science, math, or modernity. Banality is stasis and the absence of wonder.<br /> <br /> The only things that originate from the Dreaming that are immune to banality are the ancient enemies of the fae, the Fomorians. The Tuatha and their children, the Kithain, are formed of intelligence and emotions. The Fomorians predate all that and arose from primordial instinct and base survival urges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T09:13:19-07:00","id":113366,"title":"","content":"What about Slenderman? What kind of thing is he? Would he be a Fomorian, a powerful chimera, something else?<br /> <br /> Would Tommyknockers (from 1840 miners) just be a variety of knocker? They act more like Will-o'-wisps.<br /> <br /> Can there be Men-in-Black Fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2481-lordofarcana","name":"LordofArcana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T09:35:57-07:00","id":113378,"title":"","content":"It really depends on the needs of your chronicle. Slenderman could be a chimera birthed by the collective imagination of the internet. Slenderman might be a sluagh or several Kithain who served as inspiration and gain glamour off the creepy pasta. Slenderman might be a White Court Fomorian loosed on Earth, and the stories are just ways for people to rationalize away what they've seen. Slenderman could be any number of things not listed here.<br /> <br /> Just like any other RPG, Changeling: The Dreaming is limited only by your imagination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T08:55:25-07:00","id":114107,"title":"","content":"I realize that the grey aliens have had versions in other games, but I'd nominate them as another modern kith if one appeared or as a type of Chimera if they didn't.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to remember where I read it but there was actually a short story with the premise that angels, fae, and aliens were all the same creatures. That they created humanity for fun, but were killed by naked disbelief. So they buzzed humans to try to stir up belief, but if they were ever actually seen they withered and died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T23:22:47-07:00","id":114576,"title":"","content":"Some interesting speculation here. I'm of the same idea that &quot;gremlins&quot; as presented would have been some form of really nasty Chimera. Maybe even like Mage Hobgoblin sorts. If they had to be Fae I would probably make them Unseelie Knockers.<br /> <br /> When I first saw the thread title I thought it would be more Modern than WW2 and take the forms of the Quote Unquote New fads such as Steampunk Fae and Gothic Fae. Sluagh could easily slip into the Goth sterotype, and Knockers seem to comprise the steampunk element, but what of Airship flying Eshu Captains, or Troll Space Pirate Buccaneers. Maybe Western Boggan locomotive time tains? To fae in the Dreaming, especially the Deep Dreaming, time isn't always Linear, so why should time periods be? Why not have a Neon Victorian Sidhe? Maybe the Pooka thinks she's an Alien because she's part Bug and has Antennae. That's what I liked about the Changeling game, there were/are possibilities for everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T21:09:33-07:00","id":145255,"title":"","content":"I'm seeing the start of a story seed here: several people report one night that a UFO crashed nearby. Of course, nothing is found... except in the Near Dreaming! An chimera or group of chimera show up at the troupe's freehold, confused and in need of aid. What adventures transpire? And why is that nocker trying to wheel away their spacecraft? Tune in next time, true dreamers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/h38q1qmfx/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/67hc6e1i5/i_backed_ex3_small.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2045-melonlord82","name":"melonlord82","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2045_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}